// probe: c_handle - what does this engine let a plugin's own type be
// declared as, and where does it say no.
//
// What is measured here, column-exact, from the e2e launch on run
// 36726960949: "line: 5 (13) ERROR: Expected ';'" and "ERROR: Instead found
// '@'" - column 13 is the '@' itself, and line 5 was a handle declaration of
// this plugin's type. The bare spelling is refused too, and not by the
// parser: the e2e's own script, whose declaration was bare, reported
// "Parameter type can't be 'midi_output', because the type cannot be
// instantiated." and "Data type can't be 'midi_output'" (run 36730213750).
// The two refusals are different machines - a token the parser will not
// take, and a type the compiler is told not to instantiate - so each gets
// its own question, and each is still asked in isolation. Nothing runs: the
// whole question is the declaration.
#pragma plugin nvmidi

void main() {
	print("C0");
	midi_output@ a = null;
	print("C1");
	midi_output b;
	print("C2");
}
